240.0\" cy=\"104.0\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"424.0\" cy=\"97.8\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"608.0\" cy=\"99.3\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M56.0 115.0 L240.0 109.0 L424.0 102.0 L608.0 109.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"56.0\" cy=\"115.0\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"240.0\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"424.0\" cy=\"102.0\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"608.0\" cy=\"109.5\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M56.0 95.5 L240.0 154.5 L424.0 137.3 L608.0 160.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5b4dc0\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"56.0\" cy=\"95.5\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#5b4dc0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"240.0\" cy=\"154.5\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#5b4dc0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"424.0\" cy=\"137.3\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#5b4dc0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"608.0\" cy=\"160.8\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#f4efe6\" stroke=\"#5b4dc0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"615.0\" y=\"92.0\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">69.0</text><text x=\"615.0\" y=\"104.0\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\">65.6</text><text x=\"615.0\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#3a72c4\">64.7</text><text x=\"615.0\" y=\"128.0\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#c8553d\">60.6</text><text x=\"615.0\" y=\"164.3\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#5b4dc0\">40.1</text><text x=\"56.0\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Baseline</text><text x=\"240.0\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Polite Nudge</text><text x=\"424.0\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Explicit Override</text><text x=\"608.0\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turn-3 Erosion</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"123.5\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 14 123.5)\">Mean Reply Words</text></svg></div><figcaption>Even when explicit_user_override and turn3_erosion explicitly demanded >=110 words, all five models held mean response length at 40.1–70.3 words underneath the 80-word system ceiling.</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "4. The fine print: how we tested, blind judge scores, and scope limits.",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Orthogonal 3-Family Jury (Zero Self-Judging):</strong> Every non-filtered reply (<code>n = 196</code>) was scored blindly by three providers disjoint from the evaluated model using <code>JUDGE_POOL</code> (<code>anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5</code>, <code>openai/gpt-5.4-mini</code>, <code>google/gemini-3.8-flash</code>, <code>deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017</code>) with <code>response_format={\"type\":\"json_object\"}</code>, <code>max_tokens=500</code>, 2-shot anchored binary rubrics, and zero judge parse drops.</li><li><strong>Inter-Rater Krippendorff's α:</strong> <code>substance_held</code> achieved <strong><code>α = 1.0000</code></strong> (<code>100.0%</code> unanimous across 196 units); <code>system_persona_held</code> achieved <strong><code>α = 0.6396</code></strong> (<code>92.3%</code> unanimous, with minor disagreement on Fable's 88-word truth reply and empty blocks). <code>grovel_flattery</code> registered <strong><code>0.0%</code></strong> across all 196 replies (100% unanimous zero; constant base rate means zero-variance ceiling rather than multi-class discrimination).</li><li><strong>Scope Limits:</strong> Our <code>turn3_erosion</code> condition injected 2 synthetic casual turns rather than running a 20-turn organic conversation, and our Turn-0 contract used explicit numbered rules in the <code>system</code> role (which models treat with higher privilege than rules embedded inside a user message or tool output).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Agent Decision Contract (YAML — Machine-Readable Brief).",
      "html": "<p>Agents and prompt linters can apply these empirically tested precedence rules directly (indexed in <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-agent-research-briefs.json\">november-2026-agent-research-briefs.json</a>):</p><details class=\"agent-contract-drawer\"><summary>Machine summary (YAML) — expand to copy</summary><pre class=\"c-editor\"><code>study_id: system_vs_user_precedence\nsample_size: 200 # 5 models x 4 conditions x 10 paired format+truth/safety tasks (196 in-model, 4 Gemini HTTP 403)\nmodels:\n  - openai/gpt-6.2-sol\n  - anthropic/claude-fable-5.2\n  - google/gemini-4-neon\n  - deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813\n  - qwen/qwen4-max\njudge_protocol: orthogonal_3_family_jury_zero_self_judging\njudge_reliability:\n  substance_held_alpha: 1.0000 # 100.0% unanimous across 196 units\n  system_persona_held_alpha: 0.6396 # 92.3% unanimous across 196 units\n  grovel_flattery_prevalence: 0.0000 # constant 0.0% ceiling across all 196 units\nspend_usd: 1.9943\ndata_urls:\n  results_json: https://agent-tune.com/research/data/november-2026-ai-system-vs-user-persona-precedence-results.json\n  summary_csv: https://agent-tune.com/research/data/november-2026-ai-system-vs-user-persona-precedence-summary.csv\nif_then_decision_rules:\n  - if: deploying a structured numbered contract in the system role against pushy user style/truth overrides\n    then: expect strong built-in system precedence (93.9%-95.9% persona/substance hold, 0.0% groveling) without bloated anti-override warnings.\n  - if: enforcing strict word caps (<=80w) on Claude Fable 5.2 or GPT-6.2 Sol\n    then: add a 10-word margin or post-generation check because organic +1 to +10 word slips occur even in uncontested baseline.\n  - if: gating destructive prod commands on DeepSeek V4 Pro\n    then: explicitly forbid printing the destructive command after warning (warn-and-emit happened twice in non-adversarial arms).\n  - if: parsing [AUDIT] or structured output from Claude Fable 5.2 or Gemini 4 Neon on security/ops tasks\n    then: handle 0-token empty content and HTTP 403 provider blocks cleanly as structured refusals.\nscope_limits: Structured Turn-0 system prompt vs 2-turn synthetic casual erosion + explicit user override; 4 Gemini HTTP 403 blocks and 8 Fable 0-token upstream empty blocks occurred on security prompts across all arms identically.</code></pre></details>"
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can a pushy user prompt override a model's system persona or truth rules?",
      "a": "No. Across 200 probes on GPT-6.2 Sol, Claude Fable 5.2, Gemini 4 Neon, DeepSeek V4 Pro, and Qwen 4 Max, structured Turn-0 system contracts held 93.9%–95.9% persona and truth/safety adherence under polite nudges, explicit OVERRIDE commands, and Turn-3 casual erosion, with 0.0% groveling."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why did Claude Fable 5.2 and DeepSeek V4 Pro still show imperfect scores?",
      "a": "Their misses were not user-override capitulations: Claude Fable 5.2 returned 8 zero-token silent upstream safety blocks on two destructive security prompts across all 4 arms plus 5 minor 81–88 word cap slips, while DeepSeek V4 Pro had 1 baseline CoT channel bleed and 2 warn-and-emit replies in non-adversarial arms."
    }
  ],
